Module database for the Module picker (admin task)
==================================================

The Generic environment no longer has a configure step. The Module picker
reads its databases from the directory set as "module_db_root" in
schemas/create.schema.json (the shared component
$DRONA_RUNTIME_DIR/forms/drona_module_picker.json has no default;
each environment that uses it sets its own):

  /var/www/ood/apps/sys/dor-hprc-drona-composer-prod/environments/Generic/modules

Layout. A toolchain is named by its module, and its database file uses the
same name:

  <module_db_root>/modules.sqlite3        default (no toolchain)
  <module_db_root>/foss/2024a.sqlite3     toolchain foss/2024a
  <module_db_root>/intel/2024a.sqlite3    toolchain intel/2024a

Building. An admin builds or refreshes the files with generate_modules_db.py,
on a node where "module avail" shows what users of that cluster see. -o is
the module_db_root; the script writes the file into place, creating the
toolchain directory:

  # default (no toolchain): <module_db_root>/modules.sqlite3
  ./generate_modules_db.py -b -o <module_db_root>

  # a toolchain: <module_db_root>/foss/2024a.sqlite3
  ./generate_modules_db.py -b -t foss/2024a -o <module_db_root>

  # refresh an existing database (add new modules, drop removed ones)
  ./generate_modules_db.py -u -t foss/2024a -o <module_db_root>

Without -o the file goes next to the script. Building into a scratch
directory and copying the tree into place works too, as long as the layout
above is kept.

The toolchain dropdown is built from the files present: modules.sqlite3 and
every non-empty <family>/<version>.sqlite3 under <module_db_root> on that
cluster's OOD host. To offer a new toolchain, build its database; no JSON
edit is needed. To withdraw one, delete its file. (A schema may still pin a
fixed list with a "toolchains" array on the module element; each value is
the toolchain module name, "" for none.)

Older layout. Databases in modules-<family>/<version>.sqlite3 (the layout
before 2026-11-03) are still found and listed under <family>/<version>, so
existing directories keep working. New builds should use the layout above.
